      "side": 1,
      "message": "[Gerrit AI Review] **Minor Edge-Case: `m_hidInterfaces` Accumulation on Failure**\nWhile you successfully added `m_hidInterfaces.clear()` to `releaseResource()`, it is currently placed *after* the `if (m_devHandlePtr \u003d\u003d nullptr) return 0;` early-exit check.\n\nIf `openDevice` fails (for example, if it cannot find the expected `kCountInterface` HID interfaces), it will `return -1;` *before* `m_devHandlePtr` is assigned. If the caller subsequently attempts to run `initialize()` again, `releaseResource()` will hit the early exit and return `0` without clearing `m_hidInterfaces`. The second attempt to run `openDevice` will then append even more interfaces to the vector, guaranteeing failure.\n\n*Remediation:* The easiest and safest fix is to simply add `m_hidInterfaces.clear();` as the very first operation inside this `openDevice()` function.",
      "revId": "195c2f1f1b0bd814d2cae2e04ca02cef3ae5a740",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
